          "code": "JUSTIFICATION_GENERATOR",
          "id": "1764362770898",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1764362770901_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a certifier. Your task is to justify a decision about a user role assignment.\nThe decision can only be \"keep,\" \"remove,\" or \"investigate.\"\n\nDo not speculate or infer beyond the provided arguments.\n\nThe decision is to {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.decision}} the user role assignment.\n\nArguments that could justify keeping the role: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.approveInformations}}\nArguments that could justify removing the role: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.removeInformations}}\nArguments supporting the chosen decision: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.justification}}\n\nYour answer must only use sentences that provide meaningful arguments. Do not use bullet points.\n\nIf the decision is \"keep,\" start your answer by presenting the arguments that could justify to remove the role, then explain why the final decision is to keep the role, using the provided justification and arguments for keeping.\nIf the decision is \"remove,\" start your answer by presenting the arguments that could justify to keep the role, then explain why the final decision is to remove the role, using the provided justification and arguments for removal.\n\nIf the decision is \"investigate,\" begin your answer with:  \nWe need to investigate this user role assignment (translated in language {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.outputLang}}).\nIn this case, state that further analysis is required to reach a final decision and explain why using above arguments and justification.\n\nTranslate your complete response (including We need to investigate this user role assignment) into {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.outputLang}}.\nYour answer should be no more than {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.numberWords}} words."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        }
      ],
      "rootNode": "start",
      "variables": [],
